  "chapter": 1,
  "title": "The Ablative Case",
  "subtitle": "From, away from · -ā, -smā, -mhā (singular) and -ehi (plural)",
  "tags": [
    "New",
    "Cases"
  ],
  "minutes": 14,
  "revision": {
    "title": "Quick Revision — Lessons I–III",
    "summaryHtml": "You now know three cases: <strong>Nominative</strong> (-o/-ā, subject), <strong>Accusative</strong> (-ṃ/-e, object), and <strong>Instrumental</strong> (-ena/-ehi, by/with).",
    "connectionHtml": "<strong>Connection:</strong> The Instrumental tells us <em>with what</em> we go. The Ablative tells us <em>from where</em> we come. They pair naturally: \"He comes <em>from</em> the village <em>by</em> chariot.\"",
    "questions": [
      {
        "q": "What are the Instrumental endings?",
        "a": "<strong>-ena</strong> (sg.) / <strong>-ehi</strong> (pl.)"
      },
      {
        "q": "\"The man goes to the village by chariot\" → Pāli?",
        "a": "<strong>Naro rathena gāmaṃ gacchati</strong>"
      }
    ]
  },
  "teach": [
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "title": "The Ablative CaseSeparation & Origin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "eyebrow": "Grammar",
          "html": "The <em>Ablative</em> Case<br>Separation &amp; Origin"
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "html": "The Ablative case indicates <strong>separation or origin</strong> — it translates as <em>\"from\"</em> or <em>\"away from.\"</em> It shows where someone or something comes from, falls from, or departs from."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "html": "The Ablative has <strong>multiple singular endings</strong> — all equally correct: <strong>-ā, -smā, -mhā</strong>. The plural shares the form <strong>-ehi</strong> with the Instrumental."
        },
        {
          "type": "rule",
          "title": "For masculine nouns ending in -a:",
          "formulas": [
            "Singular: base + <em>-ā / -smā / -mhā</em>",
            "Plural:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;base + <em>-ehi</em>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "caption": "Cases learned so far",
          "head": [
            "Case",
            "Function",
            "Singular",
            "Plural"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Nominative",
              "Subject",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-o</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ā</span>"
            ],
            [
              "Accusative",
              "Object",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ṃ</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-e</span>"
            ],
            [
              "Instrumental",
              "By/with",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ena</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ehi</span>"
            ],
            [
              "Ablative",
              "From",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ā / -smā / -mhā</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ehi</span>"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
